&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;How should this be tested?&lt;br/&gt;
    Providing a value in zeppelin-site.xml will replace the actual Jetty server version found in HTTP Header with provided value. E.g. &lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ol&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;edit zeppelin-site.xml and add a property `zeppelin.server.jetty.name` and with value say `TOMCAT`&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;restart the server&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;open the app in browser then observe the Response Headers for the key &quot;Server&quot;  this should now reflect &quot;TOMCAT&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


